This is a file to log what files correspond to what project(s).

This file was created by Anh Mai to organize the work done over Spring and Summer 2026.



Functions : contains 3 functions to process FIA data
      - propNA : calculates the proportion of missing values by columns 
      - fia_single : reads in single FIA csvs and integrates state and research station information
      - fia_many : reads in many FIA csvs with the above information
Data : contains data for vulnerability project 
      - FIA
            - REF_SPECIES.csv : reference for FIA species
            - selected_FIA.xlsx : selected variables from large FIA datasheets, used for filtering FIA dfs
      - Trait
            - Knighton_et_al_2025.xlxs : data from random trees trained on Phylo. Eigenvector Maps found at https://zenodo.org/records/15009207
            - TRY_angio_trait.csv : TRY dataset that has been cleaned in the below .R files, only angiosperms found in the FIA
                  - 260807_FIA_exploration > 260812_TRY_data_exploration.R
                  - 260826_TRY_df_exploration.R
            - Guo_et_al_2022.txt : Imputed data values from Guo et al. (2022), https://www.pnas.org/doi/10.1073/pnas.2026733119#executive-summary-abstract
                  
                  
                  
                  
                  
260304_MLM : folder from a tutorial during JPL lab meeting by JPL.
260416_github_setup.R : connecting project to GitHub.
260417_data_loading_gbif.R : investigation of P50 values in Quercus species
    data from this is located in ~/maia1/260417_quercus_data/260419_quercus_occur_gbif
260417_quercus_data : folder to contain all GBIF files including data from the above cleaning
260420_eda.qmd : exploring P50 values from Choat et al. (2012)
    Some interesting maps of the distribution of P50 values globally and in the continental U.S.
260617_RevBayes_episodic_div_rates : practicing code from RevBayes tutorial based on primate tree
260622_SEM.R : downloaded SEM tutorial 
260731_TRY_trait_representation : looking at the table of traits to understand coverage by observation ct and by species
    More information on the top leaf, root, and floral traits in the database in the vulnerability project word doc
260807_FIA_exploration: has many files on downloading FIA data, cleaning it, and looking at TRY data in conjunction with FIA species
260826_TRY_df_exploration.R : thorough cleaning of TRY database data
260827_Knighton_cleaning.R : cleaning Knighton et al. (2025) imputed data
260827_Guo_cleaning.R : cleaning the Guo et al. (2022) imputed data

